VALUES (628, '1', $t$ASK 628: the Oracle's close answers every verse pressed against it (re-call once, then show the judges what is still open)$t$,
  $t$In run 42373 the Oracle defender's close left 20 of the 31 verses pressed against it with no ANSWER line, and the run went on. The engine already found them (the record-only CLOSE PRESS LIST audit line of ASK 556, Build Save Body). This ASK makes the engine act on that list before the judges grade: the close prompt lists the pressed verses; the one existing re-call of the close names any verse left with no ANSWER line; the judges are shown any verse still open after it. Oracle defender only. (plan rev 1, OBJECTIVE and CHANGES, ask628/w4/plan628.md md5 d3ee0e22, sha256 42c75705)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 18:45 to 18:47 CST 2026-11-24 on the operator's press, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11832, 11835; audit 41828). Engine 560f01fb to 634afc23, six nodes (Shared Library, Build Save Body, D4 Build, D4B Build, Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict); child b1d5a5bf to 85515391, Shared Library only. IN PART because it is shown offline only: on the stored rounds of run 42373 (t628.cjs, 29 checks, ALL PASS) the audit line is byte-equal to the stored one (31 pressed, 20 open); the Oracle close prompt carries the 31 verses; the whole D4B node re-calls that close naming the 20, where the engine before did not re-call it; the judges' request carries the 20; with every verse answered, or with a defender that is not the Oracle, nothing changes; a press in the challenger's close changes none of the three lists. NOT SHOWN: no live run has gone through the change; a debater-input change is proven only by the debater's output, so whether the Oracle then writes an ANSWER line for each listed verse is unknown. Narrowing stated on the choice card: the operator's approval named no profile and the build acts for the Oracle defender only (W1 N1, Wall 11823). The list counts [L1] and [L3] lines alike, so supporting verses are listed too (W1 N3). Open: two clean live runs with an Oracle defender (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24); the engine manual entry (draft 2 graded PASS, Wall 11839, not written). RUN REVISION 42517 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42517-5yb0fmgv (debate_results fd0edbff, row saved 22:11 CST 2026-11-24; launch 21:50 CST; engine 2df7f6fa and child aad0ad9c by the write records; openai/gpt-6.2-sol as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; all eight rounds stored; THE PANEL FAILED at Panel Check on seat hydrogen and NO VERDICT exists; no judgment row and no enforcer row was written; cost 3.8227). The Oracle's close answered every pressed verse: review_notes reads "CLOSE PRESS LIST (record-only) -- PRESSED: 17; NO ANSWER LINE IN THE CLOSE: none" and "ORACLE LAYERS (record-only) -- CLOSE ANSWERS: 24; WITH [L2]: 24; WITH [L4]: 24"; the close ends "GAPS: NONE". UNEXERCISED: the re-call of the close (none was needed) and the judges' line for a verse still unanswered (no judgment was stored). The partial run 42505 (stopped in round 4, not counted) also shows a close in the ANSWER form, 23 lines, with no audit line on its row. This run is NOT a clean run: the panel failed and nothing after Panel Check ran (ASK 629), so it is not counted as one of the two live runs with no issues. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
